  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0-preview.3: the four assemblies are strong-named with one key that stays fixed from here on, and an error handler now receives the exception the method threw, with its cause attached, instead of that exception's inner exception. preview.2 brought document and batch limits on by default (JsonRpcLimits), reserved method names refused at registration, InProcessClient removed, diagnostic ids on the obsolete members, and the documentation site. Since preview.1 the request pipeline is built around UTF-8 bytes, the JSON serializer is pluggable and Task and ValueTask methods are supported again, at six times the throughput of 1.2.3 through the 1.x string API and twenty-four times through the byte entry points, measured on a 32-core Hugging Face Jobs host (see the README). What is new: https://astn.github.io/JSON-RPC.NET/changelog.html. Upgrading from 1.x: https://astn.github.io/JSON-RPC.NET/upgrading.html",
